---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { AUTHOR, SITE_URL, SITE_TITLE, SITE_DESCRIPTION } from "../consts";

const links = AUTHOR.links.filter((l) => l.href);

// Periodical describes the publication. Person, linked as its author, is what
// ties the accounts together for a search engine without making the site
// itself read as a personal page.
const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "Periodical",
  name: SITE_TITLE,
  url: SITE_URL,
  description: SITE_DESCRIPTION,
  author: {
    "@type": "Person",
    name: AUTHOR.name,
    sameAs: links.map((l) => l.href),
  },
};
---

<Base title="About" description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}>
  <div class="page">
    <div class="shell">
      <span class="kicker">About</span>
      <h1>What this is</h1>

      <div class="prose column">
        <p>
          Teximos publishes writeups of production failures in working
          software. One incident per piece, with the real numbers, the code
          that caused it and what the fix actually changed.
        </p>
        <p>
          The bias is toward the failures that look boring and are not. A
          pricing table with two rows missing. A guard pointed at the wrong
          set. A transaction that protected the write and not the decision in
          front of it. These are rarely written about, because they are
          embarrassing and because they are specific, and the specifics are
          exactly what makes them useful.
        </p>
        <p>
          Nothing here is a tutorial, a framework comparison or a list. If a
          piece cannot name what broke and show the measurement, it does not
          get published.
        </p>

        <h2>Who writes it</h2>
        <p>
          {AUTHOR.name}, currently building
          <a href="https://moduspilot.com">MODUS</a>. Most of the incidents so
          far are ones caused and then fixed there, which is the only reason
          the numbers can be published in full.
        </p>
        <p>
          Corrections are welcome. If something here is wrong, it is worth
          fixing in place rather than leaving.
        </p>
      </div>

      {
        links.length > 0 && (
          <ul class="profiles">
            {links.map((l) => (
              <li>
                <span class="k">{l.label}</span>
                <a href={l.href}>{l.href.replace(/^https?:\/\//, "")}</a>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ul>
        )
      }
    </div>
  </div>

  <script
    type="application/ld+json"
    is:inline
    set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)}
  />
</Base>
